}

^["recursive_improvement"]{
 loop: [
  "? reread runtime return types and downstream consumers before widening telemetry",
  "< ship one immutable fact that removes host-side reconstruction work",
  "$ record which downstream judgment becomes cheaper: freshness, coherence, or readiness",
  "^ feed the fact into DX, governance, and docs surfaces without renaming it",
  "% never leak live mutable substrate ownership to callers",
 ]
 gates: [#immutability, #downstream_reuse, #diagnostic_alignment, #narrow_contract]
}

^["stream"]{
 # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
 # >>[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] <type> — <content>
 # Types: observe, decide, surprise, revise, blocked, taste, rebase, hygiene, implement, verify, note
 >>[2026-03-12 00:00] observe — upstream/main advanced with ea709ac, which carries valence into register metadata but does not address runtime telemetry returns.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:01] decide — keep the normalize → interpreter → register metadata path, but amend sticky valence and merged semanticFrames before building telemetry on top.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:02] decide — public runtime results should return immutable facts: events and resonances, not a live Substrate instance.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:03] hygiene — original branch memory pointed at a historical-missing base. Treat upstream commit ea709ac as design lore, not current branch baseline.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:04] taste — host apps should not reconstruct runtime telemetry outside the runtime; the API should expose canonical runtime facts directly.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:05] decide — semicolon support is desirable, but it belongs to a later seed-syntax slice rather than this runtime telemetry amendment.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:06] implement — cherry-picked upstream ea709ac in amended form, replaced sticky write semantics, and threaded immutable telemetry through runSpw() plus collectPrecipitates().
 >>[2026-03-12 00:07] verify — runtime tests, build, audit, and diff checks passed for the original telemetry amendment slice.
 >>[2026-03-12 00:08] note — `npm run lsp:smoke` still timed out on textDocument/references path-ref cases; that surface sits outside this telemetry slice.
 >>[2026-03-27 14:30] revise — regrounded branch memory to packages-era main@3b1747c4, packages/ file paths, and a branch-local artifact. Preserve upstream commit as precedent, not baseline.
 >>[2026-03-27 14:31] taste — recursive improvement here means each new runtime fact should remove a downstream guess. If a host still has to infer freshness or coherence, the contract is underpowered.
 >>[2026-03-28 16:36] observe — packages-era main already returns immutable telemetry from runSpw() and collectPrecipitates(), and ServerContext trial paths already consume telemetry-shaped results directly. The remaining drift is plan metadata, not missing runtime code.
 >>[2026-03-28 16:36] decide — resolved [freshness_shape]: keep freshness/coherence as raw runtime facts; compact readiness summaries belong to DX and governance consumers rather than the runtime payload itself.
 >>[2026-03-28 16:36] decide — resolved [lsp_projection]: LSP and editor surfaces may quote or summarize runtime events and resonances, but should not rename the underlying runtime vocabulary when turning them into diagnostics or status copy.
 >>[2026-03-28 16:36] rebase — refreshed the plan baseline to main@221128f5 and replaced the stale hot-file entry packages/spw-runtime/src/__tests__/ with the current runtime test path.
 >>[2026-03-28 16:49] note — archived under .agents/plans/_archive/runtime-telemetry-canon after confirming the telemetry contract had already landed on main and the remaining work belonged to downstream DX/editor/governance consumers.
}

